# Tells GitHub Pages to publish dist/ as-is instead of running it through Jekyll.
#
# Without this file the legacy Pages builder runs Jekyll over the whole published tree —
# 130+ MB of exam PDFs and question PNGs — on every deploy. That started failing outright
# ("Page build failed") in Sep 2026, so pushes to gh-pages stopped reaching the live site
# even though the branch itself updated correctly. Nothing here needs Jekyll: Vite has
# already produced the finished static site.
#
# Vite copies everything in public/ into dist/, and package.json's deploy script passes
# --dotfiles so gh-pages publishes this file rather than skipping it.
